{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-31079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}\\ge 5x+6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-31079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x+6 \\\\ {x}^{2}-5x-6 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-5x-6$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x-6 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/51c7484f806696105dd570684f8b194d3c1b7fc3ea27d85a1a17f53e6f7d0a64.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-5x-6\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 6.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [6,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-31079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9ddbac46468b914a6384e538c6b74dbbc2faf76205d9a70c9300014b65e2e9"} {"question" "q-31079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-31079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [6,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-6]\\cup [1,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,1]\\cup [6,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-1,6]"] ["math" "x\\in [1,6]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-31079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [6,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-142314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-142314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+x-12\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/eda4704129b905a10e379254dfd6d1ff07d593d7f97bbc6126e9d27bfec2f9f2.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-4\\le x\\le 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-142314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9ddbac46468b914a6384e538c6b74dbbc2faf76205d9a70c9300014b65e2e9"} {"question" "q-142314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-142314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2<x<3"] ["math" "-3\\le x\\le 4"] ["math" "-4\\le x\\le 3"] ["text" "$x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 4$"] ["text" "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-142314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\le x\\le 3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-276404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $6{x}^{2}+21x\\ge 12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]\\,⋃\\,[${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-276404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x & \\ge 12 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}+21x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-3x)+(24x-12) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-1)+12(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ (3x+12)(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ 3(x+4)(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/38c1897ec93625527b48ec689fbd65e9a63056e033fa6a7a0c72473f1188e7ea.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+21x-12\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]⋃[\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-276404" "field" nil 