"\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-7x\\le 0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-7x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-7x & =0 \\\\ x(x-7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=7,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/e7f9e5a051acca0be45340695fd6c2ddcb9d47936cc1f713245bd22d33151c97.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0\\le x\\le 7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9ddbac46468b914a6384e538c6b74dbbc2faf76205d9a70c9300014b65e2e9"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277263" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}-17x>-2{x}^{2}+45$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,⋃\\,(${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-17x & >-2{x}^{2}+45 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}-17x-45$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-27x)+(10x-45) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-9)+5(2x-9) & =0 \\\\ (3x+5)(2x-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=\\frac{9}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/f73c9906e6b65d1ddbda91619c7ffbb77408faa0541e2bc16565e0127d334312.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-17x-45>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x<-\\frac{5}{3}$ or $x>\\frac{9}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{3})⋃(\\frac{9}{2},\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9ddbac46468b914a6384e538c6b74dbbc2faf76205d9a70c9300014b65e2e9"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/state.json" "file_sha256" "7323fe979e92fd7b9e7e05c66a8fb9617d5d8832580827e1ad766b5019ef623f"} {"question" "q-277667" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/s